exports[`routeStoneSetFeedbackAbsorption.acceptance given: [case1] a bound route whose one peer reviewer always hands back a blocker when: [t3] the driver answers, then re-runs — and meets the STANCE gate then: matches snapshot — the composition-gate refusal: route.stone.set - composition gate refusal 1`] = `
"✋ ConstraintError: absorb each concern before you absorb counter's feedback

1 concern of counter stands un-absorbed:
  - blocker.1

absorb each, THEN absorb the feedback:
  1. per concern — concede it (the default), or dispute it:
     rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.test \\
       --as conceded --with counter --about <concern> --severity better|urgent
     rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.test \\
       --as disputed --with counter --about <concern> --why <fulcrum-path>
  2. then absorb the feedback:
     rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.test --as absorbed --that counter
"
`;

exports[`routeStoneSetFeedbackAbsorption.acceptance given: [case1] a bound route whose one peer reviewer always hands back a blocker when: [t3] the driver answers, then re-runs — and meets the STANCE gate then: matches snapshot — the stance-gate halt, as a driver reads it: route.stone.set - stance gate, concern undeclared 1`] = `
"🦉 the way speaks for itself

🦉 each concern awaits your absorption

🌕 lets declare
   │
   ├─ review.peer 1/1
   │  ├─ slug = counter
   │  └─ undeclared
   │     └─ blocker.1
   │
   ├─ why
   │  └─ a budget ends a disagreement when it runs out, not by a verdict on
   │     who is right. a stance is that verdict: you own each concern — fix
   │     it, or hold that it is fine to continue — and it goes on record
   │     where a council can rule on it.
   │
   ├─ what to do — concede, by default
   │  └─ the reviewer is right and you will fix it. that is the ordinary
   │     answer, and the sequence is: concede → fix → budget → re-arrive.
   │
   │     rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.test \\
   │       --as conceded --with <slug> --about <concern> \\
   │       --severity better|urgent
   │
   └─ what to do — dispute, to escalate
      └─ this ONE concern is fine to continue, and you want a human council
         to rule on it at the close. it costs a fulcrum entry you author and
         a human's attention, so reach for it where the concern is severe or
         recurs — never as the default.

         rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.test \\
           --as disputed --with <slug> --about <concern> \\
           --why .fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md

         1 concern stands undeclared — one command each.
"
`;

